 "poem": "The Spirit, who kept not them alive,\nWas weeping on the dead and dying,\nAnd hid His face from all unseen.\nTo him was drawn the holiest man\nWho ever in a world before\nStood up to him of God alone.\nHis hand outstretched; it came again\nUpon him at once as before;\nHe raised his face like Satan.\nThey did with him, who are alone,\nFor they saw himself not by himself.\nBy Himself, dead for ever,",
